{ Fine Isolani position |There is an option of gambitting the pawn entirely through 9...d4 , but practice has shown that it is best to restore material balance instead. White is at crossroads here, having several ways of completing development. As for our ideal piece configuration, it is quite straightforward. For the rooks, the ideal positions are generally e8 and c8 or d8, standing useful on the (semi-)open files. The real question remains for our light-squared bishop, as it might stand well on either e6, f5 or g4 depending on the situation. As usual, when playing with the isolani we should always be on the lookout for opportunities of pushing it forward at an opportune moment, as the further it advances the more of a menace it becomes to the opponent. }
